Fix BT.709 full-range color conversion with CUDA 12.

TorchCodec 0.9.1 uses NPP ColorTwist offsets that produce incorrect colors
for BT.709 full-range video with CUDA 12. Use the corrected CUDA 12 offsets
from the upstream fix.

This patch is specific to the CUDA 12.8 EasyBuild variant, so no CUDA-version
conditional is required.

Upstream issue:
https://github.com/meta-pytorch/torchcodec/issues/1262

Upstream pull request:
https://github.com/meta-pytorch/torchcodec/pull/1265

Upstream commit:
https://github.com/meta-pytorch/torchcodec/commit/80ce23c707a323effe374df36108c8b36447c716

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT5.6
diff --git a/src/torchcodec/_core/CUDACommon.cpp b/src/torchcodec/_core/CUDACommon.cpp
--- a/src/torchcodec/_core/CUDACommon.cpp
+++ b/src/torchcodec/_core/CUDACommon.cpp
@@ -149,4 +149,4 @@
 const Npp32f bt709FullRangeColorTwist[3][4] = {
-    {1.0f, 0.0f, 1.5748f, 0.0f},
-    {1.0f, -0.187324273f, -0.468124273f, -128.0f},
-    {1.0f, 1.8556f, 0.0f, -128.0f}};
+    {1.0f, 0.0f, 1.5748f, -201.5744f},
+    {1.0f, -0.187324273f, -0.468124273f, 83.8974f},
+    {1.0f, 1.8556f, 0.0f, -237.5168f}};
